  "note": "(log rho)''(x) = -1/(2x^2) - 1/(2(2-x)^2) < 0 on all of (0,2); equal to -1 at x=1. Hence rho''(mode) < 0 for every beta, and for every Gaussian: the hypothesis 'rho'' >= kappa > 0 at the centre' is empty in every exactly solvable marginal. Where rho''>0 (near the edges) the value is fixed by the Haar Jacobian, not by beta.",
